{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"SUSE-SU-2026:5251-1","published":"2026-11-16T13:19:04Z","modified":"2026-11-17T17:23:12.233445645Z","related":["CVE-2026-115557","CVE-2026-12345","CVE-2026-19445","CVE-2026-87910"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-115557","CVE-2026-12345","CVE-2026-19445","CVE-2026-87910"],"summary":"Security update for python3","details":"This update for python3 fixes the following issues:\n\nSecurity issues fixed:\n\n- CVE-2026-12345: symlinks injected during temporary directory cleanup can cause arbitrary file deletion (bsc#1283828).\n- CVE-2026-19445: reassigned SNI callbacks with unreferenced SSLContext instances can cause use-after-free\n  (bsc#1283969).\n- CVE-2026-87910: tarfile hardlink fallback ignores custom extraction filter rejection via `None`, allowing security\n  filter bypass and arbitrary file writes (bsc#1280352).\n- CVE-2026-115557: use of compromised eMudhra intermediate CA certificates in bundled pip (bsc#1287357).\n\nOther updates and bugfixes:\n\n- Require Expat 2.8.5 for Python (bsc#1285433).\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"python3","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Micro 5.3","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/python3&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Micro%205.3"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"3.6.15-150300.10.134.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"libpython3_6m1_0":"3.6.15-150300.10.134.1","python3":"3.6.15-150300.10.134.1","python3-base":"3.6.15-150300.10.134.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://ftp.suse.com/pub/projects/security/osv/SUSE-SU-2026:5251-1.json"}},{"package":{"name":"python3-core","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Micro 5.3","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/python3-core&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Micro%205.3"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"3.6.15-150300.10.134.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"libpython3_6m1_0":"3.6.15-150300.10.134.1","python3":"3.6.15-150300.10.134.1","python3-base":"3.6.15-150300.10.134.1"}]},"database_specific